KZ3 patch 2164 (RSX pass 152, renderer step 0): LD_SYNC_HIST=1 sync-point histogram (probe P4), the split of the walker time outside
the method loop ([perf-out], leaf rows under RSX_PERF + RSX_PERF_PROF), and LD_FIFO_CAPTURE=dir capture writer (format in
libs/video/rsx_fifo_capture.h). Every new path is off unless its switch is set; with the switches unset the walker's call stream is
unchanged (host test) and each hook costs one load and a predicted branch.
LD_SYNC_HIST=1 (+ LD_SYNC_HIST_N=flips per line, default 100): rsx_sync_hist.h classifies NV0039 copies, NV406E 0x6C and NV4097
0x1D70/0x1D74 releases, flips with a dirty main-surface write-back, reports and SET_REFERENCE per flip and prints draws between
consecutive resolve points, a chunk estimate (seal at each sync event and each 128 draws) and a summary at exit ([sync-hist] lines).
[perf-out]: outside-loop remainder (walk - meth) = lock + pre + sema (before-sync inside) + park + flipword + eop (submit inside) + rest;
present-wait (ld_present_slot) is counted inside the method loop (sink_flip), shown separately.
LD_FIFO_CAPTURE=dir with a 'work' path segment (+ LD_FIFO_CAPTURE_FRAME=start,count): walker words, renderer guest_ptr reads
(first-sight bytes), walker guest reads and writes, NV0039/NV3089 copies, SPU notes and drains, initial IO/VRAM images.
Host tests tools/smoke/test_sync_hist.sh, tools/smoke/test_fifo_capture_format.sh.

